In article <HAIRSTON.90Dec11140753@henry.ece.cmu.edu> hairston@henry.ece.cmu.edu (David Hairston) writes:
>[gaston@drycas.club.cc.cmu.edu writes:]
>
>[] Should a blessed potion of speed make the intrinsic permanent, in the
>[] same way that a blessed potion of invisibility works?
>
>debatable ...

Speed is intrinsic in some characters anyway, and since you can get for example
the same teleport control as a wizard from eating a tengu etc. there should be 
at least something that gives intrinsic speed.  I don't like the idea blessing 
all your potions to get intrinsics of all of them, but there again you do get 
'intrinsic' stat increases.  Speed is more important than a single stat however,
and should be difficult to obtain.

In Larn (since there is no rec.games.larn I'll mention it here) we have a spell
called per-permanence(sp?)  this can only be cast once per book found with it
in, but any abilities you have from reading scrolls, drinking potions etc.
automatically become intrinsic!  Maybe that might be useful.

